{
  "about": "Shared now-playing geometry, in pixels relative to the Tile. The Companion encodes covers to the art box, and the Firmware, the app preview and the Companion hit-test taps with the part zones, so all three must produce these values. art = min(h - 2*pad, floor((w - 2*pad) * 2 / 5), art_max), and no art below art_min; the art box sits pad from the left, centered vertically. The text column starts pad after the art, or at pad without art, and ends pad before the right edge. The controls row shows when h >= row_min_tile_h and the text column is at least row_min_text_w wide: it is row_h tall, pad above the bottom edge, and split into previous, play_pause and next, each floor(text_w / 3) wide with the remainder on next. Without the row, the whole Tile is play_pause. A zone holds x from its x up to but not including x + w, and the same for y. With state 0 (nothing playing) no tap names a part. Whoever changes a constant regenerates these vectors.",
  "constants": {
    "pad": 20,
    "art_max": 256,
    "art_min": 48,
    "row_h": 56,
    "row_min_tile_h": 200,
    "row_min_text_w": 180
  },
